00:09:03.901 --> 00:09:05.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:05.701 --> 00:09:09.567
-That was amazing. Aah! Gosh.

00:09:09.567 --> 00:09:11.167
I was waiting. I knew --
Alright.

00:09:11.167 --> 00:09:12.767
I'm working on it.
Alright? Yeah.

00:09:12.767 --> 00:09:14.601
-You know what?
It's a stand-up thing.

00:09:14.601 --> 00:09:17.067
Stand-up comedy is like --
I have a lot of funny ideas.

00:09:17.067 --> 00:09:18.467
Just give us the funniest ones.

00:09:18.467 --> 00:09:19.868
We don't want to hear
anything else.

00:09:19.868 --> 00:09:22.033
-Edit.
-Edit. Edit everything.

00:09:22.033 --> 00:09:24.200
-Edit a conversation.
-Right. Edit your closet.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:25.501
-Yeah.
-Edit your life.

00:09:25.501 --> 00:09:27.167
-Yeah.
-Edit everything down.

00:09:27.167 --> 00:09:30.133
-And then so you did that,
and then it wasn't even on --

00:09:30.133 --> 00:09:32.400
It was before streaming or any
of the stuff, when you were --

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:34.300
-Yeah, I just put it
on the Internet,

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:39.934
and I just put it on a website
and I just left it there and...

00:09:39.934 --> 00:09:41.300
-It just grew from there.
-Yeah.

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:44.501
-We did -- One of my favorite
memories of my life

00:09:44.501 --> 00:09:46.434
was hanging out with you.
We did --

00:09:46.434 --> 00:09:49.133
We were in a great car that kept
breaking down, by the way.

00:09:49.133 --> 00:09:50.801
Do you remember that?
-The car?

00:09:50.801 --> 00:09:52.501
Oh, The Corvette broke down.
It a '54 Corvette.

00:09:52.501 --> 00:09:54.167
-And people thought it was
the funniest thing,

00:09:54.167 --> 00:09:55.667
watching Jerry Seinfeld
stall in the car.

00:09:55.667 --> 00:09:57.200
-Yeah, I got very frustrated.
Yeah.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:58.968
People were like,
"That's Jerry Seinfeld.

00:09:58.968 --> 00:10:01.234
He can't start the car!"

00:10:01.234 --> 00:10:02.834
Old women
were laughing at us.

00:10:02.834 --> 00:10:06.067
-But then we got to go
in my Boston Whaler.

00:10:06.067 --> 00:10:08.400
The world's greatest boats.
-Yes.

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:09.934
-Boston Whalers.
-I ended up getting --

00:10:09.934 --> 00:10:11.901
-And you got one
because you loved mine.

00:10:11.901 --> 00:10:14.834
-Yes. I got it because
I was in that thing.

00:10:14.834 --> 00:10:17.200
And I go, "This is unbelievable.
Do you use it?"

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:18.434
And you go, "I like this."

00:10:18.434 --> 00:10:20.234
-Yeah. I have a 13-foot
Boston Whaler.

00:10:20.234 --> 00:10:21.868
You know those little boats?

00:10:21.868 --> 00:10:24.133
It's the Unsinkable Legend,
is their brand --

00:10:24.133 --> 00:10:25.734
is the hook for their brand.
-Yes.

00:10:25.734 --> 00:10:27.667
-Because you can cut
a Boston Whaler into pieces,

00:10:27.667 --> 00:10:29.534
and it still floats.
-Which I plan to do.

00:10:29.534 --> 00:10:31.434
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:31.434 --> 00:10:33.501
And then I thought,
"He's the unsinkable legend."

00:10:33.501 --> 00:10:35.334
You know how he has
this amazing,

00:10:35.334 --> 00:10:38.133
unnatural enthusiasm
every night?

00:10:38.133 --> 00:10:40.133
He's -- Every night.

00:10:40.133 --> 00:10:42.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:42.634 --> 00:10:44.501
You are the unsinkable legend.
-No, you are.

00:10:44.501 --> 00:10:45.934
You are the greatest.
Thank you.

00:10:45.934 --> 00:10:48.334
You always give you a good
nickname every time you come on.

00:10:48.334 --> 00:10:49.667
-Yeah.
-Yeah. The Unsinkable Legend

00:10:49.667 --> 00:10:51.033
is what I'm gonna go
with this time.

00:10:51.033 --> 00:10:52.501
-Right, or
the White Snow Leopard.

00:10:52.501 --> 00:10:54.734
-Snow Leopard
was a different one.

00:10:54.734 --> 00:10:57.400
Guys, "The Comedians in Cars
Getting Coffee Book"

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:59.133
is out right now.

